1 """
2 GPT Engineer workflow definition and execution
3 
4 This module provides the necessary utilities and functions to orchestrate the execution of GPT-engineer's tasks
5 related to code generation, execution, and review. It leverages a flexible approach to system prompt creation,
6 workflow execution, and interaction with AI, allowing for various configurations and stages of operation.
7 
8 Imports:
9 - Standard libraries: inspect, re, subprocess
10 - Additional libraries/packages: termcolor, typing, enum
11 - Internal modules/packages: langchain.schema, gpt_engineer.core, gpt_engineer.cli
12 
13 Key Features:
14 - Dynamic system prompt creation for both new code generation and improving existing code.
15 - A series of utility functions for handling various tasks like AI code generation, user clarification,
16   code execution, and human review.
17 - Configurable workflow steps to control the process of code generation and execution in different scenarios.
18 - Flexibility to adapt to different configurations and use cases.
19 
20 Classes:
21 - Config: An enumeration representing different configurations or operation modes for the workflow.
22 
23 Functions:
24 - setup_sys_prompt(dbs: DBs) -> str: Creates a system prompt for the AI.
25 - setup_sys_prompt_existing_code(dbs: DBs) -> str: System prompt creation using existing code base.
26 - curr_fn() -> str: Returns the name of the current function.
27 - lite_gen(ai: AI, dbs: DBs) -> List[Message]: Runs the AI on the main prompt and saves results.
28 - simple_gen(ai: AI, dbs: DBs) -> List[Message]: Runs the AI on default prompts and saves results.
29 - clarify(ai: AI, dbs: DBs) -> List[Message]: Interacts with the user for clarification.
30 - gen_clarified_code(ai: AI, dbs: DBs) -> List[dict]: Generates code after clarification.
31 - execute_entrypoint(ai: AI, dbs: DBs) -> List[dict]: Executes code entry point and asks user for confirmation.
32 - gen_entrypoint(ai: AI, dbs: DBs) -> List[dict]: Generates entry point based on information about a codebase.
33 - use_feedback(ai: AI, dbs: DBs): Uses feedback from users to improve code.
34 - set_improve_filelist(ai: AI, dbs: DBs): Sets the file list for existing code improvements.
35 - assert_files_ready(ai: AI, dbs: DBs): Checks for the required files for code improvement.
36 - get_improve_prompt(ai: AI, dbs: DBs): Interacts with the user to know what they want to fix in existing code.
37 - improve_existing_code(ai: AI, dbs: DBs): Generates improved code after getting the file list and user prompt.
38 - human_review(ai: AI, dbs: DBs): Collects and stores human review of the generated code.
39 
40 Constants:
41 - STEPS: A dictionary that maps the Config enum to lists of functions to execute for each configuration.
42 
43 Note:
44 - This module is central to the GPT-engineer system and its functions are intended to be used in orchestrated
45   workflows. As such, it should be used carefully, with attention to the correct order and sequence of operations.
46 """
